Inventory in mdj format (markdown with JSON). ais ignores this text, because
it is above the first level 1 heading.

- One level 1 heading for each system or product.
- Directly below the heading: one JSON block with the definitive values.
- Level 2 headings: free text. "## Usage" becomes the field "usage", and
  "## Interest" becomes the field "interest". The task's field policy
  decides what the model sees of each field.
- A product without a device record has no hostname and no ip. Without a
  version, every supported version is watched.

# fw01.cyberdyne.systems

```json
{
  "hostname": "fw01.cyberdyne.systems",
  "ip": "10.1.0.1",
  "site": "earth",
  "vendor": "Palo Alto Networks",
  "product": "PAN-OS",
  "version": "11.1.4",
  "owner_email": "netops@cyberdyne.systems"
}
```

## Usage

Edge firewall, internet facing. No GlobalProtect VPN and no other services on
the internet facing interfaces. The management interface is firewall protected.

## Interest

Only critical and high findings with an unauthenticated remote attack vector.

